		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=3085#p3085"><![CDATA[
I wasn't really sure where to put this, I hope I got it right.<br><br>While using Force to control a character in an FPS, I noticed that when walking around, I wasn't always moving in the direction I was facing. I narrowed it down to the friction. When I turned friction on the materials to 0, it worked fine, but everything was slippery. recorded a demonstration to a quicktime movie. <a href="http://members.shaw.ca/chasey/media/FrictionProblems.mov" class="postlink">http://members.shaw.ca/chasey/media/Fri ... oblems.mov</a><br><br>The blue line shows where it should have gone, red where it did.<br><br>I hope that this is just temporary, and will be fixed by 2.43.<br><br>Oh, I almost forgot, object damping doesn't work anymore.<br><br>Thank you for reading!<br>-Chaser<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=1504">Chaser</a> — Fri Jan 05, 2007 6:45 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
